"""AQS-CTL-002 control philosophy and PLC architecture (X-CTL-02, A-M-194). One PLC per sector; I/O from AQS-CTL-001 (AI, LSH DI)
and AQS-INV-004 electronics (DI points, starters, contactors and solenoid drivers as DO, VFD speed references as AO, BLDC and stepper
drivers on the fieldbus). Modules of 16 channels with 20 % spare. Life-support and energy sectors get a redundant CPU pair and dual
24 V supplies (redundancy rule); all PLCs on an IEC62439_2 MRP ring; programs in IEC61131_3 structured text in the repo (X-CTL-04).
Run: python3 docs-authority/_plc_arch.py"""
import csv, math, os, sys, collections, json
R = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); os.chdir(R); sys.path.insert(0, R)
from flow_graph.param.refs import cite
for k in ('IEC62439_2', 'IEC61131_3', 'IEC61131_2', 'NFPA72_2025'): cite(k)
SPARE, CH, W_MOD, W_CPU = 0.20, 16, 2.0, 12.0
# Sectors whose PLC gets a redundant CPU pair, each with the reason. A sector is here when losing its controller would put the
# occupants, their air, water or food, or the plant power at risk before the controller can be repaired.
CRIT = {
    'HAB': 'the occupied habitat',
    'FARM': 'food and the grow-bed air loop of the habitat',
    'NUT': 'nutrient dosing of the grow beds (FARM)',
    'WTR': 'drinking water and sanitation for the occupants',
    'CRYO': 'oxygen and hydrogen storage and the habitat air handling',
    'GAS': 'the hydrogen and oxygen headers and their relief',
    'ELEC': 'plant power and the critical bus (PV, flow battery, genset and fuel cell are ELEC units)',
    'PUMPED_HYDRO': 'the backup energy store of the critical bus',
    'GEO': 'the ground-source heat pumps',
}
# Sectors kept on a single CPU by decision, with the reason (AQS-OQ-001).
SINGLE_BY_DECISION = {
    'HEAT': 'owner decision 2026-10-24 (AQS-OQ-001 Q-014): HEAT holds the insulated thermal stores (Q1 to Q4 tiers) and '
            'their heat exchangers. A controller outage stops heat moving between the stores; the stores keep their heat, '
            'losing only their standing loss. It is not a life-support or power function.',
}
assert not set(CRIT) & set(SINGLE_BY_DECISION)
io = collections.defaultdict(collections.Counter)
for r in csv.DictReader(open('docs-authority/inventory/INSTRUMENT_INDEX.csv')): io[r['sector']]['AI' if 'AI' in r['signal'] else 'DI'] += 1
MAP = {'PLC digital I/O point': 'DI', 'motor starter (contactor + overload)': 'DO', 'compressor contactor + overload': 'DO', 'solenoid driver channel': 'DO', 'variable-frequency drive': 'AO', 'BLDC driver': 'BUS', 'stepper driver': 'BUS'}
for r in csv.DictReader(open('docs-authority/inventory/OTHER_INVENTORY.csv')):
    if r['category'] == 'electronics' and r['item'] in MAP and r['sector'] != 'CONTROL': io[r['sector']][MAP[r['item']]] += int(r['qty'])
rows = []; T = collections.Counter()
for s in sorted(io):
    c = io[s]; mods = {k: math.ceil(c[k]*(1 + SPARE)/CH) for k in ('AI', 'AO', 'DI', 'DO')}; red = s in CRIT
    W = (sum(mods.values())*W_MOD + W_CPU*(2 if red else 1))
    rows.append((s, c, mods, red, W)); T.update(c); T['mods'] += sum(mods.values()); T['W'] += W
md = ['# Control philosophy and PLC architecture', '', 'Document number: AQS-CTL-002', 'Revision: B', 'Date: 2026-10-25',
      'Authority: AQS-PLAN-007 task X-CTL-02; assumption A-M-194. Generated by `docs-authority/_plc_arch.py` from the instrument index AQS-CTL-001 and the inventory AQS-INV-004; do not edit this page by hand. Study.', '',
      '| Rev | Description | Date |', '|---|---|---|', '| A | First issue | 2026-10-16 |',
      '| B | Purpose and scope added; text rewritten to the documentation style guide (AQS-DOC-002). No controller, point count or decision changed. | 2026-10-25 |', '',
      '## 1. Purpose and scope', '',
      'The plant is run by programmable logic controllers (PLCs), which read the instruments and drive the pumps, valves and other actuators. '
      'This page states the control philosophy: how the controllers are divided, which of them are duplicated, how safety and fire functions are '
      'kept apart from basic control, and how the controllers are networked and programmed. It then counts the input and output (I/O) points of '
      'each controller and sizes its I/O modules and its 24 V supply.', '',
      '## 2. Control philosophy', '',
      '- Each sector has its own PLC, so that a fault in one sector stays in that sector. The plant runs from the set-points in the flow graph. Every control loop is a single-input, single-output proportional-integral (PI) loop unless the design of the unit calls for a cascade.',
      '- A sector whose controller, if lost, would put the occupants, their air, water or food, or the plant power at risk before it could be repaired has a redundant pair of central processing units (CPUs). The pair switches over without a bump in the outputs, and it has two 24 V supplies fed from the critical bus, which is backed by a stored-energy supply to NFPA 111. These sectors and the reasons are listed in Table 3.1. Every other sector has a single CPU.',
      '- Safety trips are not part of the basic control PLCs. They are handled by the safety functions of task X-CTL-03, which follow the hazard and operability study (HAZOP) of task X-SAF-01. The fire alarm is a separate panel to NFPA72_2025; it sends signals to the PLCs and never receives them.',
      '- All PLCs, the operator screens (HMIs) and the data historian are on one fibre-optic ring using the Media Redundancy Protocol (MRP) of IEC62439_2. A single cut in the ring is recovered within 200 ms. Brushless DC (BLDC) motor drivers and stepper drivers are on a fieldbus within each sector.',
      '- The programs are written in IEC61131_3 structured text, kept in the repository, and simulated against the flow graph before they are loaded into the controllers (task X-CTL-04).', '',
      '## 3. Redundant CPU pairs', '',
      'Table 3.1 lists the sectors whose PLC has a redundant CPU pair.', '',
      'Table 3.1. Sectors with a redundant CPU pair', '',
      '| Sector | Why its controller is redundant |', '|---|---|'] + [f'| {s} | {why} |' for s, why in sorted(CRIT.items())] + [
      '', 'The following sectors are kept on a single CPU by decision of the project owner:', ''] + [f'- {s}: {why[0].upper() + why[1:]}' for s, why in sorted(SINGLE_BY_DECISION.items())] + ['',
      '## 4. Input and output points and modules', '',
      f'Table 4.1 counts the analogue inputs (AI), analogue outputs (AO), digital inputs (DI), digital outputs (DO) and fieldbus drives of each PLC, and the number of I/O modules needed. Each module has {CH} channels, and {SPARE*100:.0f} % of the channels are kept spare. The last column is the load of the PLC on its 24 V supply.', '',
      'Table 4.1. I/O and modules by PLC', '',
      '| Sector PLC | AI | AO | DI | DO | Fieldbus drives | Modules AI/AO/DI/DO | CPU | 24 V load W |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
md += [f"| PLC-{s} | {c['AI']} | {c['AO']} | {c['DI']} | {c['DO']} | {c['BUS']} | {m['AI']}/{m['AO']}/{m['DI']}/{m['DO']} | {'redundant pair' if red else 'single'} | {W:.0f} |" for s, c, m, red, W in rows]
md += [f"| Total | {T['AI']} | {T['AO']} | {T['DI']} | {T['DO']} | {T['BUS']} | {T['mods']} modules | {sum(1 for r in rows if r[3])} redundant of {len(rows)} | {T['W']:.0f} |", '',
       f"The control system draws about {T['W']/1000:.2f} kW from the 24 V supplies, which is within the critical load of AQS-ELEC-007.", '',
       'The module count in AQS-INV-004 (item OF-07) uses a different basis, the number of points divided by 16 with no spare, and is superseded by Table 4.1. The DI count adds the high-level switches of the instrument index to the digital points of the inventory. If the inventory already counts those switches, the DI count is 113 too high, which errs on the safe side.']
open('docs-authority/CONTROL_ARCH.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(md) + '\n'); print(dict(T))
